@* Every /admin address no page claims, malformed identifiers included - "/admin/library/abc" does not
   satisfy the :guid constraint, so it lands here as well. Without it endpoint routing found nothing and
   answered an empty 404, and the router's own NotFound content was never reached: that only renders for
   an interactive router, and this one is static (see App.razor). A catch-all ranks below every literal
   and constrained route, so no real page or controller action is shadowed. *@

@page "/admin/{*path}"

<PageNotFound>There is no admin page at this address.</PageNotFound>

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public string? Path { get; set; }
}
